The xlsx skill is authored by the ultrawork project. It is not derived from Anthropic's
proprietary document skills, nor from any of the third-party skill collections surveyed
in docs/discussions/059 §2 — SKILL.md, scripts, fixtures and capabilities.json are
written from scratch (see docs/discussions/059 §5 L0 for the clean-room gate that
checks this, including an AST-skeleton fingerprint that survives renaming).

It invokes the following third-party software at runtime (NOT bundled; installed by the
user per the SKILL.md instructions):
  - openpyxl (MIT)
  - lxml (BSD-3-Clause)
  - LibreOffice / soffice (MPL-2.0), invoked as an external command

The ECMA-376 element orderings encoded in scripts/office/xmlorder.py are taken from the
published standard (ECMA-376 Part 1, §18.3.1), which is a specification of fact.
